0.15 0.18 0.24 rg
BT /F1 9.8 Tf 54.00 546.39 Td (   Computes exact calendar years, months, and days by accounting for variable month lengths) Tj ET
0.15 0.18 0.24 rg
BT /F1 9.8 Tf 54.00 532.59 Td (\(calendar.monthrange\) and leap years \(calendar.isleap\), alongside total elapsed seconds) Tj ET
0.15 0.18 0.24 rg
BT /F1 9.8 Tf 54.00 518.79 Td (\(elapsed_seconds = t_now - t_birth\).) Tj ET
0.15 0.18 0.24 rg
BT /F1 9.8 Tf 54.00 500.99 Td (2. Synodic Lunar Phase Algorithm \(calculate_moon_phase\):) Tj ET
0.15 0.18 0.24 rg
BT /F1 9.8 Tf 54.00 483.19 Td (   Uses the astronomical synodic month constant \(S = 29.530588853 days\) anchored to the reference New) Tj ET
0.15 0.18 0.24 rg
BT /F1 9.8 Tf 54.00 469.39 Td (Moon epoch of January 6, 2000 at 18:14 UTC:) Tj ET
0.15 0.18 0.24 rg
BT /F1 9.8 Tf 54.00 451.59 Td (   - Cycle Position \(phi\) = \(\(t_birth - t_epoch\) mod S\) / S \(ranging from 0.0 to 1.0\)) Tj ET
0.15 0.18 0.24 rg
BT /F1 9.8 Tf 54.00 433.79 Td (   - Illumination \(%\) = \(\(1 - cos\(2 * pi * phi\)\) / 2\) * 100) Tj ET
0.15 0.18 0.24 rg
BT /F1 9.8 Tf 54.00 415.99 Td (3. Planetary Orbital Age Calculation:) Tj ET
0.15 0.18 0.24 rg
BT /F1 9.8 Tf 54.00 398.19 Td (   Divides total Earth days lived \(D_lived\) by each planet's heliocentric orbital period P_planet) Tj ET
0.15 0.18 0.24 rg
BT /F1 9.8 Tf 54.00 384.39 Td (\(Mercury: 87.969 d, Venus: 224.701 d, Earth: 365.256 d, Mars: 686.980 d, Jupiter: 4332.589 d, Saturn:) Tj ET
